      "key": {
        "uuid": "4b881cf3_082ab1cd",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-28T17:43:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not sure I understand. For DoH to be in effect, it has to follow its particular pattern. I don\u0027t see a case where DoT and DoH would be using the same URL?",
      "parentUuid": "a45d4ed7_6e3e467e",
      "revId": "528d633d21988272c64b1e094d075b1ab5d2fc1b",
      "serverId": "35266860-6252-469c-a67d-185064479fc0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6a78badf_47644580",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000062
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-28T17:48:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like this change doesn\u0027t accept a URL; it comes up with one on its own based on the typical URLs used. So, for example, we could have DoT available via `dns.calyxos.org` while also having DoH available via `https://dns.calyxos.org/dns-query`. This approach would try the latter first and use it if available, but previously it would only try DoT.\n\nThat has always bothered me about AOSP\u0027s presentation of Private DNS, because users may have a reason to prefer either DoT or DoH, and with Android, they don\u0027t really get a choice. The closest thing they\u0027ve had to a choice is to select something other than Google (or Cloudflare), in which case they\u0027re effectively choosing DoT. With this, it sounds like there\u0027s no choice, if both services use the same domain.",
      "parentUuid": "4b881cf3_082ab1cd",
      "revId": "528d633d21988272c64b1e094d075b1ab5d2fc1b",
      "serverId": "35266860-6252-469c-a67d-185064479fc0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b2455871_6df1f862",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-28T18:02:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, if the same domain is used for both then it seems like DoH would be favoured over DoT since they both make use of the same UI",
      "parentUuid": "6a78badf_47644580",
      "revId": "528d633d21988272c64b1e094d075b1ab5d2fc1b",
      "serverId": "35266860-6252-469c-a67d-185064479fc0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "486b2183_ad0fa5ff",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-29T12:05:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So then this patch does force DoH, and thus it\u0027s not \"Allow all DoH providers\", and more \"Force DoH if available for provider\".\n\nThat\u0027s not good. But then again, we shouldn\u0027t change the basic Android UI, so that doesn\u0027t leave many good options here.",
      "parentUuid": "b2455871_6df1f862",
      "revId": "528d633d21988272c64b1e094d075b1ab5d2fc1b",
      "serverId": "35266860-6252-469c-a67d-185064479fc0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9d59daa8_32a55f85",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000062
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-30T14:33:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The URL we are generating in this patch isn\u0027t part of [RFC 8484](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8484) - `/dns-query` is commonly used, but not guaranteed. Today, browsers that allow you to configure DoH require you to give them a full URL. See Mullvad\u0027s guide as an example: https://mullvad.net/en/help/dns-over-https-and-dns-over-tls#browsers\n\nSo, rather than guessing at the URL, couldn\u0027t we just accept a full URL, and then if the user-provided string starts with https://, use DoH with what they gave us?",
      "parentUuid": "486b2183_ad0fa5ff",
      "revId": "528d633d21988272c64b1e094d075b1ab5d2fc1b",
      "serverId": "35266860-6252-469c-a67d-185064479fc0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b2bf68e0_118193a3",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-30T15:26:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I don\u0027t see any issues with that.\n\nNow:\nIf I put \u0027dns.google\u0027 -\u003e DoH / default AOSP behavior?\n\nProposed:\ndns.google -\u003e DoT\nhttps://dns.google/dns-query -\u003e DoH\n\nThat does change things wrt stock Android but making it clear in the process, which sounds ok.",
      "parentUuid": "9d59daa8_32a55f85",
      "revId": "528d633d21988272c64b1e094d075b1ab5d2fc1b",
      "serverId": "35266860-6252-469c-a67d-185064479fc0"
